#!/usr/bin/env bash
#
# survey — send the local model to read the repository, and bring back something checkable.
#
#   tools/survey --task <task.md> --repo <dir> --out <dossier.json> [--provider native]
#
# ## Why this exists
#
# Measurement put 84% of the orchestrator's cost in planning, and about 89% of THAT in deciding
# rather than writing. The route this project built moved implementation to the local model —
# the remaining 16% — and then added a review phase on top, which is how it arrived at 2.0x the
# tokens and 4.3x the wall clock of simply doing the work. We automated the typing. Typing was
# never the cost.
#
# The cost is reading. Deciding what to change requires holding the repository in context, and a
# stateless conversation re-sends every file it has read on every subsequent turn, so planning
# cost is context accumulation rather than thought. Reading is exactly what is free on a machine
# you already own.
#
# ## Why it is not simply "let the local model plan"
#
# Implementation was safe to delegate because it had a gate: acceptance criteria run mechanically,
# so a bad round is a DETECTED bad round and a re-roll costs GPU time instead of correctness.
# Reading has no such gate, and a dossier that is confidently wrong is worse than no dossier —
# the orchestrator decides on false premises with no signal that anything is off. Eight of nine
# rejections on the first feature were defects in the specification, written by the party that had
# actually read the files. Handing reading to a 20B model without a gate makes that surface worse.
#
# What makes it tractable is that a dossier, unlike a decision, is machine-checkable. Every claim
# it may contain is one of three shapes — a verbatim quote, a replayable search, or a path — and
# all three are checkable without judgement. tools/dossier-verify is that gate, and it is the
# whole reason this is a schema and not a free-text brief.
#
# ## What this is NOT allowed to do
#
# It does not design, and it does not write code. The schema gives it no field for either, in the
# same way and for the same reason consult.schema.json gives the orchestrator no field in which to
# weaken a criterion: the party being checked does not get to choose the measurement.
#
# The write tools are left registered rather than disabled. Disabling them means editing
# native-agent, which changes harness_tree and stops every future implementation run from pooling
# with the corpus already collected — a real cost for no gain here, because the dossier is scored
# against a pristine checkout regardless of what the model does to its own worktree.

set -uo pipefail

HERE="$(cd "$(dirname "$(readlink -f "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")")" && pwd)"
HANDOFF_HOME="$(cd "$HERE/.." && pwd)"

TASK=""; REPO=""; OUT=""; PROVIDER="native"; LOG=""

while (( $# > 0 )); do
    case "$1" in
    --task)     TASK="$2"; shift 2 ;;
    --repo)     REPO="$2"; shift 2 ;;
    --out)      OUT="$2"; shift 2 ;;
    --provider) PROVIDER="$2"; shift 2 ;;
    --log)      LOG="$2"; shift 2 ;;
    -h|--help)  sed -n '2,40p' "$0"; exit 0 ;;
    *) echo "survey: unknown option: $1" >&2; exit 64 ;;
    esac
done

[[ -f "$TASK" ]] || { echo "survey: no task file at ${TASK:-<unset>}" >&2; exit 66; }
[[ -d "$REPO" ]] || { echo "survey: no repo at ${REPO:-<unset>}" >&2; exit 66; }
[[ -n "$OUT"  ]] || { echo "survey: --out is required" >&2; exit 64; }
[[ -f "$HANDOFF_HOME/providers/${PROVIDER}.sh" ]] || { echo "survey: unknown provider: $PROVIDER" >&2; exit 64; }

mkdir -p "$(dirname "$OUT")"
[[ -n "$LOG" ]] || LOG="${OUT%.json}.log"
mkdir -p "$(dirname "$LOG")"

read -r -d '' DEV <<'DEV' || true
You are surveying a code repository. You are not implementing anything and you are not designing
anything: someone else will decide what to build, and they will decide it using only what you
bring back. They cannot see this repository. You are their eyes.

Answer only the schema.

Three rules, because your answer is checked by machine before anyone reads it:

1. QUOTE, NEVER RECALL. Every quote you give is compared byte-for-byte against the file you name.
   Read the file, copy the text out of what you read, and paste it. A quote that is close but not
   exact is treated as a fabrication, and one fabrication voids the whole dossier.

2. RECORD THE COMMANDS YOU RAN. Your searches are re-run against a clean checkout and the files
   they return are compared with the files you say they returned. Write the command exactly as
   you ran it.

3. AN UNKNOWN IS AN ANSWER. If you cannot determine something, put it in `unknowns` and move on.
   You are not scored on confidence. A guess that reads like a finding is the single most
   expensive thing you can hand back, because the planner has no way to tell it apart from a
   fact you verified.

Be exhaustive about `change_surface` in particular. The plan written from this dossier will be
permitted to touch only the files you name, so a file you fail to find is a file the
implementation cannot use — it will not be discovered later, it will simply be missing.
DEV

PROMPT="Survey this repository for the task below. Do not implement it.

## The task

$(cat "$TASK")

## How to go about it

Start by finding where this area of the codebase lives — search for the domain words in the task,
then read what the searches turn up. Follow the code outward: when a file you read calls something
you do not recognise, find it. Look for how the codebase already solves problems of this shape,
because the plan should match the neighbours rather than invent a style.

Then find the tests that already cover this area, and work out what commands would prove the task
was finished. A proving command must FAIL today — if it passes on the tree as it stands, it is not
measuring the change.

Stop when reading more stops changing your answer, and submit the dossier. Do not stop earlier
because you have enough for a plausible summary: the person reading this cannot open a single one
of these files, and everything you leave out is simply lost."

(
    HANDOFF_ROLE=surveyor
    export HANDOFF_ROLE
    # shellcheck disable=SC1090
    source "$HANDOFF_HOME/providers/${PROVIDER}.sh"
    if declare -F provider_preflight >/dev/null && ! provider_preflight; then
        exit 3
    fi
    provider_run "$REPO" "$HANDOFF_HOME/schemas/survey.schema.json" "$OUT" "$LOG" "$DEV" "$PROMPT"
) >>"$LOG" 2>&1

[[ -s "$OUT" ]] || { echo "survey: the model returned nothing (see $LOG)" >&2; exit 2; }
python3 -c "import json,sys;json.load(open(sys.argv[1]))" "$OUT" 2>/dev/null \
    || { echo "survey: the dossier at $OUT is not JSON (see $LOG)" >&2; exit 2; }
echo "$OUT"
